# Gimnasio de Pueblo Cantera (M5-D, contract 26;: the Rock gym), 12 x 14, interior, column = i, row = j, (0,0) = back corner.
# The floor is the user's pick "G3": one big slab per 2 x 2 cells, so the tile of a cell depends on the parity of (i, j): the grid characters 0 1 2 3 are slab_<i%2><j%2>
# (0 = i even / j even ... 3 = both odd); the cells of an object / NPC use the letter of THEIR parity (pillar P Q R T, boulder e f g h, guide u, apprentice x) so the joint lines
# run through them like everywhere else. Garrick stands on his dais (stage, 2 x 2, cells (5..6, 1..2); he is at (6,1), the far-right cell; the stage is a counter, so the hero talks to him from (6,3) across the dais, and is not in front of him on the screen; he faces the entrance = SW). A row of pillars and boulders
# (j = 8) leaves a 2-wide gap at i = 5, 6; the boulder at (6,7) shuts the way around it, so every way to Garrick passes (5,7), on the line of sight of the apprentice at (3,5)
# (facing S, range 2: he sees (4,6) and (5,7)): like the usual Jr. Trainer, he cannot be avoided (the host test `m5` proves it with a flood fill). The guide is by the door.
@map gimnasio_cantera
@size 12 14
@interior yes
@bg 3
@fill slab_11
@spawn door 5 12 N
@flag badge_cantera 80          # the Medalla Cantera (party.h FLAG_BADGE_FIRST)
@flag garrick_disc 696         # (contract 80): Garrick handed over Disc 36. 696 = the pick-up flag of the pouch that lay in Pueblo Cantera until contract 80, so an old save that took it keeps it taken
@legend
  0  tile=slab_00
  1  tile=slab_10
  2  tile=slab_01
  3  tile=slab_11
  C  tile=none object=wall_corner
  w  tile=none object=wall_j
  |  tile=none object=wall_i
  P  tile=slab_00 object=pillar
  Q  tile=slab_10 object=pillar
  R  tile=slab_01 object=pillar
  e  tile=slab_00 object=boulder
  f  tile=slab_10 object=boulder
  g  tile=slab_01 object=boulder
  s  tile=none object=stage
  G  tile=none object=stage npc=garrick id=garrick face=SW script=garrick
  u  tile=slab_10 npc=guia id=guide face=NW script=guide
  x  tile=slab_11 npc=aprendiz id=apprentice face=S trainer=aprendiz_cantera range=2 text=tr.aprendiz_cantera.pre after=tr.aprendiz_cantera.after
  m  tile=mat
@grid
  Cwwwwwwwwwww
  |3232sG32323
  |1010ss10101
  |3R3232323R3
  |10101010101
  |32x23232323
  |10101010101
  |32323g32323
  |QefP10QefeQ
  |32323232323
  |1P1010101P1
  |32323232323
  |101010u0101
  |3232mm32323

@warp m -> pueblo_cantera spawn=gym_door
# The gym guide.
@script guide npc
    npc_face_hero guide
    jf badge_cantera won
    say cantera.gym.guide.a
    end
  won:
    say cantera.gym.guide.b
@end
# Garrick: before the badge he speaks, battles (trainer garrick: Pebblump L12 + Boulderback L14); a win = his speech, the badge (flag 80), the explanation;
# a loss = the normal blackout to the last Centro. Afterwards he only says his last line.
@script garrick npc
    jf badge_cantera after
    npc_face_hero garrick
    cam_npc garrick             # the camera cuts to him: from the floor his head would be above the top of the screen
    say cantera.garrick.pre
    battle 6 0                  # trainer 6 = garrick (position in assets/data/trainers.toml); var 0 = 1 won / 0 lost
    jv 0 1 won
    blackout
    end
  won:
    say cantera.garrick.win
    setf badge_cantera
    say cantera.badge
    say cantera.garrick.about
    call garrick_gift
    cam_hero
    end
  after:
    npc_face_hero garrick
    cam_npc garrick
    jf garrick_disc said
    call garrick_gift
    cam_hero
    end
  said:
    say cantera.garrick.after
    cam_hero
@end
# (contract 80): after the badge he hands over a disc (here Disc 36, the Hold Fast role: Contencion). A full bag keeps garrick_disc clear and he hands it over the next time you talk to him.
@script garrick_gift called
    jf garrick_disc gone          # an old save that took the pouch (or a disc already handed over): nothing more
    say gym.varo.disc
    give_item disc_36 1
    jv 0 0 full
    item_var 0 disc_36
    say gl.gift
    setf garrick_disc
    say extra.garrick.disc_about
    end
  full:
    say gl.found.full
  gone:
@end
